WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:05.560
While you were fighting Rennala, did you ever
wonder what words her children were singing?It's

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:10.679
hard to make out with all the chaos going
on around you..but if we extract the voice

00:00:10.679 --> 00:00:23.779
files from this fight, then we can hear, and
read this: Sleep tight, bound tight by Mother's

00:00:23.779 --> 00:00:26.480
amber."Mother's amber" is Rennala's amber
egg.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:32.660
Within this egg is the Great Rune of the Unborn
- a shard of the Elden Ring given to her by

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:35.020
Radagon, her former husband.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:39.690
With it, she rebirths juvenile scholars over
and over again.

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:45.670
According to the Juvenile Scholar Set, "Rebirth
is as sleep to them, and with each awakening,

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:50.820
memory fades into oblivion".

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:58.510
Hence the lullaby.Sleep tight, find life,in
Mother's umbra.Umbra is basically another

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:00.530
word for "shadow".

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:05.680
Specifically though, umbra often refers to
the region of darkest shadow during a lunar

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:06.680
eclipse.

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:10.180
All of a sudden, this line becomes hugely
poetic.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:14.690
Rennala is the Queen of the Full Moon..and
her children are being reborn in her umbra

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:17.580
- the shadow of her moon.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:19.200
(NOTE: This symbolism of eclipse rebirth is
also paralleled in Sol)This game is overflowing

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.250
with beautiful secrets and deep hidden meanings..and
I think these secrets videos are a great format

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:22.250
to share them with you all.

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:23.250
What's crazy, as always, are the little details
that From Software place into their games.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:24.250
Did you know, for example..that Rennala's
Queen's Set gauntlets hide a small secret?

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:29.120
When you equip these, you don't just equip
the bracelets..you equip a tiny ring on your

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:30.780
little finger, as well.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:34.990
Now, I'm probably reading too much into it
- but it's been documented that wearing a

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:41.760
single ring on the little finger can "advertise
the possession of a costlier piece of apparatus

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:47.560
put away in store"..and that's certainly the
case with Rennala, whose boss room has a locked

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:50.990
chest containing Ranni's Dark Moon Ring.

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:56.380
This is a ring of betrothal, "supposed to
be given by Lunar Princess Ranni to her consort".

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:59.460
THIS ring was locked away by Princess Ranni
herself.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:04.900
The warning engraved upon the ring reads "Whoever
thou mayest be, take not the ring from this

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:05.900
place.

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:09.369
The solitude beyond the night is better mine
alone.".

00:02:09.369 --> 00:02:13.530
With this ring, you can become Ranni's consort,
and unlock a new ending.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:18.280
The ring goes on to say that "Ranni is an
Empyrean, and any consort of hers would by

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.120
rights earn the title of lord".

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:28.859
So obviously, betrothal was an important concept
to the Royal Family - and doubly so, for Ranni.

00:02:28.859 --> 00:02:33.430
According to the Dark Moon Greatsword, "it
is long-standing tradition for a Queen of

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:38.279
Caria to bestow a Moon Greatsword upon her
spouse".

00:02:38.279 --> 00:02:43.319
As such, you receive the Dark Moon Greatsword
when Ranni takes you as her consort at the

00:02:43.319 --> 00:02:46.530
end of her questline.

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:55.180
Now..Rennala was once betrothed to Radagon
- so where then, is his Moon Greatsword?

00:02:55.180 --> 00:03:06.299
Well..it's been lost in the consecrated snowfields,
wielded by a misbegotten.

00:03:06.299 --> 00:03:08.309
It's this, the Golden Order Greatsword.

00:03:08.309 --> 00:03:10.519
Doesn't look like a moon greatsword does it?

00:03:10.519 --> 00:03:12.799
Well..that's because it used to be one.

00:03:12.799 --> 00:03:16.930
"Greatsword made of light, modeled after the
Elden Ring itself.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:22.219
Forged by King Consort Radagon to proudly
symbolize the tenets of the Golden Order.

00:03:22.219 --> 00:03:27.659
Telltale signs betray that this was once the
greatsword bequeathed to him by his first

00:03:27.659 --> 00:03:32.549
wife, Rennala."

00:03:32.549 --> 00:03:35.730
So it wasn't just forged - it was reforged.

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:40.639
Radagon fought for the Golden Order, but then
married Rennala and was given a Moon Greatsword.

00:03:40.639 --> 00:03:46.239
Then, when he left Rennala to return to the
Golden Order, he reforged his Moonlight Greatsword

00:03:46.239 --> 00:04:10.650
into the Golden Order Greatsword instead.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:15.329
At the back of Rennala's room she keeps a
statue of Radagon, despite him leaving her

00:04:15.329 --> 00:04:16.900
so long ago.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:20.859
This is the same statue design that was commissioned
for the Erdtree capital.

00:04:20.859 --> 00:04:24.949
The same statue that reveals that Radagon
is in fact..Marika.

00:04:24.949 --> 00:04:28.050
If you're not familiar with the concept of
Radagon being Marika, you should go and watch

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:30.090
my previous lore video.

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:40.090
It lays the groundwork for all the lore I'll
be discussing in the videos to come.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:48.800
But what I want to talk about isn't the statue
exactly - rather, it's the backing of the

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:49.800
statue.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:51.669
This criss-cross pattern.

00:04:51.669 --> 00:04:56.110
This mesh is actually crazy important to Radagon
as a character.

00:04:56.110 --> 00:05:00.490
It's like his seal.

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:01.490
His symbol.

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:02.490
His..Elden Rune.

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:07.460
And it is something you notice EVERYWHERE,
once you start looking for it.

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:13.479
For example, Radagon's Scarseal is "An eye
engraved with an Elden Rune"..and his mesh

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:15.530
pattern is sealed on it.

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:19.810
Next, we see this same pattern on the door
that blocks access to the Erdtree.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:26.099
Of course, Radagon is inside at this point
- and his seal is a part of what prevents

00:05:26.099 --> 00:05:27.319
you from entering.

00:05:27.319 --> 00:05:33.599
Next we find it on the Mask of Confidence,
in gold thread sown over the mouthpiece in

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:35.370
a crossed fashion.

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:43.520
It reads: "When Radagon married Rennala, he
ordered the Carian magic preceptors to don

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:44.830
these masks.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:49.650
To make it clear that all of their matters
were to be kept strictly private".

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:53.440
As you probably know, Radagon was indeed keeping
a lot of secrets.

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:58.139
I want to thank Quelaag, whose work on the
lore I respect a lot, for pointing out the

00:05:58.139 --> 00:05:59.220
masks to me!

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:06.510
And finally, this pattern is found..on the
main menu, and the Elden Ring itself.

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:09.819
So why does the Elden Ring have Radagon's
seal upon it?

00:06:09.819 --> 00:06:14.300
Well..this is probably a new element added
when Radagon became the vessel for the Elden

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:15.879
Ring.

00:06:15.879 --> 00:06:18.020
It's now housed within him.

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:22.750
It makes some sense then that his seal..would
be represented upon the symbol of the Elden

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:25.090
Ring, in some way.

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:27.720
But what does Radagon's mesh represent?

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:36.340
It's very orderly, like Radagon himself - so
I do think the character is represented in

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:43.759
the design..and the Scarseal item clarifies
"These seals represent the lifelong duty of

00:06:43.759 --> 00:06:56.099
those chosen by the gods".

00:06:56.099 --> 00:07:01.729
The stronger version of the Scarseal is the
Soreseal, and it reads "Solemn duty weighs

00:07:01.729 --> 00:07:07.659
upon the one beholden; not unlike a gnawing
curse from which there is no deliverance."

00:07:07.659 --> 00:07:14.210
The red seals on these eyes become so embedded
that their shape becomes barely recognisable.

00:07:14.210 --> 00:07:18.139
A heavy duty, indeed.

00:07:18.139 --> 00:07:20.879
Of course, Marika has seal talismans as well.

00:07:20.879 --> 00:07:27.830
And as with Radagon, the talismans reveal
the shape of her seal - hers is a crucifix.

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:30.849
You would have seen this crucifix all throughout
the Lands Between.

00:07:30.849 --> 00:07:34.350
It's present in every area because the crucifix
is the symbol of the summoning pool, but you'll

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:39.979
find a ton of crucifixes in Limgrave especially,
where there are countless undying, screaming

00:07:39.979 --> 00:07:41.629
bodies pinned up.

00:07:41.629 --> 00:07:46.099
I'll admit - I'm not sure why these bodies
only scream at night, nor why they've been

00:07:46.099 --> 00:07:48.810
punished in this way..not why they're smouldering..nor
why they're undying, even after you release

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:49.810
the rune of death.

00:07:54.417 --> 00:07:59.577
You could interpret this as her being in shackles
for shattering the Elden Ring, as the Elden

00:07:59.577 --> 00:08:05.268
Beast also likes to punish us with a crucifix
of its own - but beyond these shackles, it's

00:08:05.268 --> 00:08:09.108
undeniable that this pose became a symbol
of her entire reign.

00:08:09.108 --> 00:08:13.318
For example, go and look at the statues of
Marika throughout the game.

00:08:13.318 --> 00:08:19.108
All feature her with her hands flung out,
almost as if she's mimicing the shape of the

00:08:19.108 --> 00:08:30.018
rune of death..This woman, this god, removed
death from the land, and I think this posture

00:08:30.018 --> 00:08:35.418
is the symbol of that blessing, and her seal.

00:08:35.418 --> 00:08:40.078
The vertical line coming down through the
center of the Elden Ring is present in almost

00:08:40.078 --> 00:08:47.048
all of the Great Runes symbols, and it really
helps in aligning them all together to form

00:08:47.048 --> 00:08:48.698
the shape of the Elden Ring.

00:08:48.698 --> 00:08:50.678
Something like this, perhaps?

00:08:50.678 --> 00:08:57.358
But how many Great Runes do you really need
to complete the Elden Ring?

00:08:57.358 --> 00:09:00.958
Well..there would have been a point in your
playthrough where the Two Fingers tell you

00:09:00.958 --> 00:09:06.388
that you only need to collect Two Great Runes
to earn the right to become Elden Lord, and

00:09:06.388 --> 00:09:07.978
to restore the Golden Order.

00:09:07.978 --> 00:09:10.428
You might have thought this was strange right?

00:09:10.428 --> 00:09:14.618
How can the Elden Ring be complete with just
two Great Runes?

00:09:14.618 --> 00:09:19.948
Well remember: Morgott guards the Erdtree..he's
not an optional boss at all..and with his

00:09:19.948 --> 00:09:27.608
Great Rune..you have three - and the Elden
Ring starts to look pretty complete at that

00:09:27.608 --> 00:09:28.608
point.

00:09:28.608 --> 00:09:29.608
Complete enough to restore order, apparently.

00:09:29.608 --> 00:09:33.958
In fact, even if you get every Great Rune
in the game and theoretically fully restore

00:09:33.958 --> 00:09:39.438
the Elden Ring - it's possible that it's still
not really complete.

00:09:39.438 --> 00:09:45.908
For example, In Faram Azula, there's an even
bigger Elden Ring..with even more rings.

00:09:45.908 --> 00:09:53.608
Nothing explicitly mentions this Mega Elden
Ring, so speculation is all we have.

00:09:53.608 --> 00:09:58.338
My best guess at this stage is that maybe
this is some primordial form of the Elden

00:09:58.338 --> 00:09:59.338
Ring?

00:09:59.338 --> 00:10:04.348
Since it has more rings, maybe this is something
that existed in an earlier age?

00:10:04.348 --> 00:10:09.208
As for the roots, I kind of interpret this
as the way the Mega Elden Ring's blessings

00:10:09.208 --> 00:10:11.948
might have been filtered down to the world?

00:10:11.948 --> 00:10:14.378
In a more natural way, perhaps?

00:10:14.378 --> 00:10:24.288
Elden Ring will almost certainly receive DLC
- so I wouldn't be surprised if we were able

00:10:24.288 --> 00:10:26.648
to collect more Great Runes in the future.

00:10:26.648 --> 00:10:30.618
From a gameplay point of view it makes sense
- there is a system for equipping Great Runes

00:10:30.618 --> 00:10:31.998
in the game, after all.

00:10:31.998 --> 00:10:37.728
But from a lore point of view - we do know
of at least one other Great Rune that we haven't

00:10:37.728 --> 00:10:38.728
found yet.

00:10:38.728 --> 00:10:39.728
Ranni's.

00:10:39.728 --> 00:10:46.268
Ranni is said to have cast aside her Great
Rune,

00:10:46.268 --> 00:10:54.708
There was a really interesting post a little
while ago by reddit user FlintVonEverec who

00:10:54.708 --> 00:10:59.859
proposed that Ranni's Great Rune could have
been hidden on the moon itself which..I mean

00:10:59.859 --> 00:11:05.868
it just makes so much sense, considering who
she is.

00:11:05.868 --> 00:11:06.868
Amazing theory.

00:11:06.868 --> 00:11:07.868
Amazing find.

00:11:07.868 --> 00:11:12.238
I remember noticing that shape on the moon
so long ago in promotional material for the

00:11:12.238 --> 00:11:17.258
game, and it's crazy to think this symbol
might have ended up having a meaning like

00:11:17.258 --> 00:11:18.338
this.

00:11:18.338 --> 00:11:23.068
Another thing that we speculated about before
the game was officially released..was this

00:11:23.068 --> 00:11:25.488
line of dialogue, from Margitt.

00:11:25.488 --> 00:11:29.978
Cower in fear of the night.

00:11:29.978 --> 00:11:35.328
The hands of the Fell Omen shall brook thee
no quarter.

00:11:35.328 --> 00:11:39.558
Now that the game is released, I think we
have an explanation for why he says this.

00:11:39.558 --> 00:11:43.378
The hands of the Fell Omen might just be the
Night Cavalry.

00:11:43.378 --> 00:11:48.768
According to their set "The Night's cavalry,
who now wander the dim roads of night, were

00:11:48.768 --> 00:11:50.438
once led by the Fell Omen".

00:11:50.438 --> 00:11:55.838
That said, the set makes it clear that they
USED to be led by the Fell Omen, and that

00:11:55.838 --> 00:11:57.588
they're not any more.

00:11:57.588 --> 00:12:00.798
So take it with a grain of salt, I guess.

00:12:00.798 --> 00:12:05.698
In fact, you should always be taking what
I say with a grain of salt - especially in

00:12:05.698 --> 00:12:08.798
these early days, as we're all still figuring
out the lore.

00:12:08.798 --> 00:12:14.108
For example, since posting my recent Lore:
Explained video, I've developed my own theories

00:12:14.108 --> 00:12:20.158
further, and read and listened to some much
needed criticisms.

00:12:20.158 --> 00:12:26.308
So, to prevent a couple of outdated theories
spreading I've actually gone and spliced out

00:12:26.308 --> 00:12:29.458
some problematic sections of that video in
the YouTube editor.

00:12:29.458 --> 00:12:35.309
If you haven't watched that video, I still
maintain that it's worth watching - but in

00:12:35.309 --> 00:12:39.658
case you have watched that video already,
I'm going to take some time now to update

00:12:39.658 --> 00:12:43.128
you all on how my ideas have changed.

00:12:43.128 --> 00:12:48.168
First off, there's a small part in the previous
video where I call the Erdtree a parasite.

00:12:48.168 --> 00:12:52.198
So..first - parasite was just the wrong word
to use.

00:12:52.198 --> 00:12:57.608
Calling it parasitic almost characterises
the Erdtree as sinister just for feeding off

00:12:57.608 --> 00:13:00.348
an energy source, which is..wrong, obviously.

00:13:00.348 --> 00:13:01.968
It's a tree.

00:13:01.968 --> 00:13:02.968
That's what trees do.

00:13:02.968 --> 00:13:03.968
It's probably wrong to characterise the Erdtree
at all, to be honest.

00:13:03.968 --> 00:13:10.318
In the words of Quelaag, another lore creator
- the Erdtree is more symbiotic, if anything.

00:13:10.318 --> 00:13:12.588
Symbiotic is a good word, I think.

00:13:12.588 --> 00:13:18.458
Because we know the Erdtree was symbiotic
with one thing at least - the Great Tree.

00:13:18.458 --> 00:13:26.628
Root Resin tells us that "the Erdtree's roots
were once entwined with that of the Erdtree".

00:13:26.628 --> 00:13:32.138
In my video I also put forward that the Great
Tree was where the crucible of life was located..and

00:13:32.138 --> 00:13:38.338
that this Great tree and this power source
was likely what the Erdtree drew upon for

00:13:38.338 --> 00:13:39.338
power.

00:13:39.338 --> 00:13:43.478
Now, I still don't think I'm necessarily wrong
on this, but I should have better shown my

00:13:43.478 --> 00:13:45.668
reasoning for this statement in the video.

00:13:45.668 --> 00:13:50.758
So, now I'd like to point out, if only briefly,
that my main piece of evidence for the Great

00:13:50.758 --> 00:13:56.678
Tree being the location of the crucible of
life, is Crucible Knight Siluria's Tree Helm.

00:13:56.678 --> 00:14:01.668
This is a "crucible" helmet..that features
"Great tree ornamentation".

00:14:01.668 --> 00:14:05.798
To me, if these knights of the crucible were
fashioning their gear after the Great Tree

00:14:05.798 --> 00:14:09.808
specifically..then that's a fairly strong
connection, to me, that the crucible is linked

00:14:09.808 --> 00:14:10.978
to the Great Tree.

00:14:10.978 --> 00:14:15.388
However, it bears mentioning that no item
descriptions explicitly link the crucible

00:14:15.388 --> 00:14:22.018
with the Great Tree..it's all indirect evidence
- so bear that in mind.

00:14:22.018 --> 00:14:28.428
Next, I should have elaborated when I said
that Marika killed the Fell God.

00:14:28.428 --> 00:14:29.428
She didn't.

00:14:29.428 --> 00:14:33.928
Rather, as per the One-Eyed Shield, it's "believed"
that she killed the fell god.

00:14:33.928 --> 00:14:37.919
Of course, other descriptions like "flame
of the fell god" make it clear that "the fell

00:14:37.919 --> 00:14:44.918
god still lurks within the Fire Giants", and
we'll go more into detail on that later.

00:14:44.918 --> 00:14:50.038
She certainly suppressed the power of the
Fell God..you could say she defeated it - but

00:14:50.038 --> 00:14:52.298
it's clearly still a force in the world.

00:14:52.298 --> 00:14:58.898
and lastly, I've removed the statement that
Malenia and Miquella were born after the shattering.

00:14:58.898 --> 00:15:11.588
This was said under the assumption that they
must have been born from a single conjoined

00:15:11.588 --> 00:15:16.108
god after the shattering, but of course, you
can also choose to believe that they were

00:15:16.108 --> 00:15:22.668
born of Radagon and Marika before they were
conjoined post-shattering, and I actually

00:15:22.668 --> 00:15:28.148
think that's the more likely option at this
point, so yeah - these twins were very likely

00:15:28.148 --> 00:15:31.058
born before the shattering.

00:15:31.058 --> 00:15:37.708
I also no longer believe the divine towers
were built after the shattering, and I've

00:15:37.708 --> 00:15:40.218
removed that point from the video as well.

00:15:40.218 --> 00:15:43.348
So thank you, to those who critiqued me politely.

00:15:43.348 --> 00:15:45.578
I'm always happy to admit that I'm wrong.

00:15:45.578 --> 00:15:46.578
It means I'm learning.

00:15:46.578 --> 00:15:51.858
So I'm going to make more of an effort to
have my scripts peer reviewed, in the future.

00:15:51.858 --> 00:16:12.948
So I'm not All Knowing.

00:16:12.948 --> 00:17:12.088
Not yet, anyway.

